linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux - Git at Google","url":"https://kernel.googlesource.com/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux/%2B/9d83e1f05c98bab5de350bef89177e2be8b34db0/sound/soc/codecs/tas2781-i2c.c"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"www.spinics.net","ref_id":"turn10search9","snippet":"# [PATCH 6.16 147/183] ALSA: hda: tas2781: reorder tas2563 calibration variables ... * In-reply-to: <20250907195615.802693401@linuxfoundation.org> ... commit d5f8458e34a331e5b228de142145e62ac5bfda34 u","title":"[PATCH 6.16 147/183] ALSA: hda: tas2781: reorder tas2563 calibration variables — Linux Stable Kernel Updates","url":"https://www.spinics.net/lists/stable/msg869880.html"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"lists.openwall.net","ref_id":"turn10search10","snippet":"李则良 <lizeliang.linux@...il.com> 于2026年8月15日周六 02:19写道： ... > During runtime resume from power-saving states, the tas2781 amplifier","title":"linux-kernel - Re: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2781: Add delay before block checksum retry to prevent deadlock","url":"https://lists.openwall.net/linux-kernel/2026/08/14/1642"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"git.ti.com","ref_id":"turn10search11","snippet":"| index : tas2781-linux-drivers/tas2781-linux-driver | [Select] [Input] ... * | Upload tas2781 register setting for BT speaker HEAD master | Ding | 2025-04-22 | 1","title":"tas2781-linux-drivers/tas2781-linux-driver - Unnamed repository; edit this file 'description' to name the repository.","url":"https://git.ti.com/cgit/tas2781-linux-drivers/tas2781-linux-driver/log/"},{"type":"text_result","domain":"isomer-user-content.by.gov.sg","ref_id":"turn10search12","snippet":"<tr><td>CVE-2025-39696</td><td>In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved: ALSA: hda: tas2781: Fix wrong reference of tasdevice_priv During the conversion to unify the calibrat","title":"<table id=\"e1\">","url":"https://isomer-user-content.by.gov.sg/36/9fc2c84b-6fdd-4a41-b0c9-2b1ac3c83a86/10_Sep_2025.pdf"}]}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_25","type":"command_execution","command":"/usr/bin/bash -lc '/home/gon7187/.agents/skills/swarm/swarm.sh post /home/gon7187/Projects/Omarchy-LenovoYogaBook9/.swarm/20261002-162703-141463 a2 \"Critical independent finding: installed 7.2.5 module tasdevice_config_put disassembly only clamps, locks, updates tas_priv->cur_conf, unlocks; no DSP call. Mainline identical. Thus Config Id 1 then 0 with no intervening OPEN does NOT force reload, especially post-OPEN. Force Firmware Load is persistent flag tested on OPEN by select_tuningprm_cfg, invalidating per-device cur_conf and forcing program/config/calibration reload. Datasheet p10 idle currents estimate two amps only ~0.07-0.13 W at 8-12V (mode dependent), far short of observed 0.65W. Runtime PM get_sync held whole PCM OPEN prevents amp runtime suspend while PCM alive.\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
